      "rationale": "WorkOrderly operates in SMB Workforce Scheduling — the same core functional category as Cadence (field-service scheduling and dispatch for SMB service businesses). Both products target the same buyers (SMB service business operators) and solve the same primary problem (scheduling and workforce coordination), making simultaneous investment highly problematic."
    },
    {
      "company": "FieldForce",
      "type": "direct",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "rationale": "FieldForce operates in Field Operations, which directly overlaps with Cadence's sector (B2B SaaS / Field Service Management). Both target field operations workflows for service businesses, and the fund holding both would create a direct intra-portfolio conflict with competing portfolio companies serving identical customer segments and use cases."
    },
    {
      "company": "SwiftSchedule",
      "type": "direct",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "rationale": "SwiftSchedule is an Appointment Booking platform — scheduling is the primary function Cadence delivers. Both target SMB service businesses that need to schedule jobs and appointments. The product overlap is substantial enough that holding both would create direct competition within the portfolio."
    },
    {
      "company": "RouteIQ",
      "type": "adjacent",
      "severity": "manageable",
      "rationale": "RouteIQ provides logistics routing software, which overlaps with the dispatch component of Cadence's platform. Field-service dispatch typically includes route optimization, meaning Cadence and RouteIQ address adjacent parts of the same workflow. Customers of one are strong prospects for the other, creating awkward portfolio dynamics, though the core products differ."
    },
    {
      "company": "ServiceBridge",
      "type": "adjacent",
      "severity": "manageable",
      "rationale": "ServiceBridge operated in Field Service Management — the same sector as Cadence — but has exited. The conflict is historical rather than active; however, the fund's deep familiarity with this space from ServiceBridge may inform (rather than block) the Cadence investment."
    },
    {
      "company": "ClearCRM",
      "type": "customer_overlap",
      "severity": "manageable",
      "rationale": "ClearCRM targets SMB companies with a CRM product. SMB service businesses — Cadence's core customer segment — are heavy CRM users, meaning both companies pursue the same buyer. The product categories are distinct (CRM vs. scheduling/dispatch), but the shared SMB service business customer base creates notable overlap."
    },
    {
      "company": "InvoiceAI",
      "type": "customer_overlap",
      "severity": "manageable",
      "rationale": "InvoiceAI serves SMB businesses with fintech/invoicing tools. SMB field service companies (Cadence's target) also need invoicing, so both products share the same SMB service business customer segment. Products are complementary rather than competing, but the shared customer base creates mild portfolio dynamics to manage."
    }
  ]
}
